From: NixOS config <root@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/ttm: don't leave the bulk_move cursor dangling

Fixes a use-after-free of ttm_lru_bulk_move_pos::first/last, which
corrupts the TTM manager LRU and wedges the machine in a soft lockup
(native_queued_spin_lock_slowpath on bdev->lru_lock) inside
amdgpu_cs_ioctl, making the session completely unresponsive.

ttm_resource_add_bulk_move() only adds a resource to its bo's
bulk_move cursor while the resource is evictable, but it can become
unevictable (pinned or swapped) afterwards. ttm_resource_del_bulk_move()
was gated on !ttm_resource_unevictable(), so a removal that ran while
the resource was unevictable - notably ttm_bo_set_bulk_move() at BO
teardown, or ttm_resource_free() - was silently skipped, leaving
pos->first/pos->last pointing at the resource. Once it was freed, the
next ttm_resource_add_bulk_move() on that cursor read the dangling
pos->first->bo->base.resv (the WARN at ttm_resource.c:235) and then
list_move()d through freed memory.

Reachable here as: a BO is swapped out by memory pressure
(ttm_bo_shrink) or by ttm_device_prepare_hibernation() during the
hibernate freeze, stays on its VM's bulk_move cursor, is closed after
resume (amdgpu_vm_bo_del -> ttm_bo_set_bulk_move), and the next
hibernation swapout corrupts the LRU. Observed on Lenovo 83DD
(HawkPoint1, 780M/890M, amdgpu e65a020e6011) with
linux-cachyos-bore-lto 7.2.4: 21x WARNING ttm_resource.c:235 during the
S4 freeze, then a 26s soft lockup on CPU#11 in ttm_resource_manager_usage
under Hyprland.

Track actual cursor membership with a new ttm_resource::bulk_move flag so
removal always undoes the matching addition, regardless of any pin/swap
transition in between, and take resources off the cursor before parking
them on bdev->unevictable. Same approach as Samuel Ainsworth's "drm/ttm:
fix bulk_move cursor use-after-free for unevictable resources" (closes
drm/amd#5387), adapted to this tree, which already carries
ttm_resource_del_bulk_move_unevictable() but still reaches the cursor
only through the evictable-gated path.

Signed-off-by: zeph <root@localhost>
---
--- a/include/drm/ttm/ttm_resource.h
+++ b/include/drm/ttm/ttm_resource.h
@@ -274,6 +274,15 @@
 	 * @lru: Least recently used list, see &ttm_resource_manager.lru
 	 */
 	struct ttm_lru_item lru;
+
+	/**
+	 * @bulk_move: Whether this resource is currently tracked by its bo's
+	 * &ttm_lru_bulk_move cursor. Recorded when the resource is added, so that
+	 * the matching removal also happens when the resource has since become
+	 * unevictable (pinned or swapped) - otherwise the cursor's first/last
+	 * pointers would be left dangling at a freed resource.
+	 */
+	bool bulk_move;
 };
 
 /**
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/ttm/ttm_resource.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/ttm/ttm_resource.c
@@ -280,16 +280,32 @@
 void ttm_resource_add_bulk_move(struct ttm_resource *res,
 				struct ttm_buffer_object *bo)
 {
-	if (bo->bulk_move && !ttm_resource_unevictable(res, bo))
+	if (bo->bulk_move && !ttm_resource_unevictable(res, bo)) {
 		ttm_lru_bulk_move_add(bo->bulk_move, res);
+		res->bulk_move = true;
+	}
 }
 
 /* Remove the resource from a bulk move if the BO is configured for it */
 void ttm_resource_del_bulk_move(struct ttm_resource *res,
 				struct ttm_buffer_object *bo)
 {
-	if (bo->bulk_move && !ttm_resource_unevictable(res, bo))
+	/*
+	 * Remove based on whether the resource was actually added, not on its
+	 * current evictability: a resource can become unevictable (pinned or
+	 * swapped) after being added, and must still be taken off the bulk_move
+	 * cursor before it is freed - otherwise pos->first/pos->last are left
+	 * dangling at freed memory and the next add or move on that cursor
+	 * corrupts the manager LRU.
+	 *
+	 * bo->bulk_move is re-checked because a resource can be moved to a
+	 * fresh BO by ttm_transfer_object_init() without ever being taken off
+	 * the old BO's cursor; that case is left alone, as before.
+	 */
+	if (res->bulk_move && bo->bulk_move) {
 		ttm_lru_bulk_move_del(bo->bulk_move, res);
+		res->bulk_move = false;
+	}
 }
 
 /*
@@ -301,8 +317,7 @@
 					    struct ttm_buffer_object *bo)
 {
 	WARN_ON_ONCE(!ttm_resource_unevictable(res, bo));
-	if (bo->bulk_move)
-		ttm_lru_bulk_move_del(bo->bulk_move, res);
+	ttm_resource_del_bulk_move(res, bo);
 }
 
 /* Move a resource to the LRU or bulk tail */
@@ -314,9 +329,16 @@
 	lockdep_assert_held(&bo->bdev->lru_lock);
 
 	if (ttm_resource_unevictable(res, bo)) {
+		/*
+		 * Take the resource off the bulk_move cursor first: it is no
+		 * longer part of that range once it lands on the unevictable
+		 * list, and leaving it tracked would dangle the cursor when the
+		 * resource is freed.
+		 */
+		ttm_resource_del_bulk_move(res, bo);
 		list_move_tail(&res->lru.link, &bdev->unevictable);
 
-	} else if (bo->bulk_move) {
+	} else if (res->bulk_move && bo->bulk_move) {
 		struct ttm_lru_bulk_move_pos *pos =
 			ttm_lru_bulk_move_pos(bo->bulk_move, res);
 
@@ -352,6 +374,7 @@
 	res->bus.is_iomem = false;
 	res->bus.caching = ttm_cached;
 	res->bo = bo;
+	res->bulk_move = false;
 
 	man = ttm_manager_type(bo->bdev, place->mem_type);
 	spin_lock(&bo->bdev->lru_lock);
